# CapCut Batches

When a campaign or main-image job needs CapCut renders, **do not ask Vadim whether CapCut is open
or to bring it to the front.** CapCut is open. Bring it forward yourself and start shooting:

```bash
osascript -e 'tell application "CapCut" to activate'
./<batch>.sh <keys...>   # run in the background
```

- No confirmation prompts (no AskQuestion "is CapCut in front?") before or during a batch.
- If the batch logs "waiting for CapCut in front", re-run the `activate` line yourself; do not ask.
- Only stop and tell Vadim if CapCut is not running at all or the batch fails three times.

## Product mains on white

Product card mains are both (or all) real packs on a pure white canvas, nothing else, as on product 30
(`problemcream_v2/main.jpg`). Build the reference from the real cut-outs on white at that scale (tallest
pack about 74% of the frame height, group centred, bottoms at 90%), re-shoot it in CapCut, check every
label at full size, and export under a new filename.
